{
  "description": "The application follows a client-server architecture, primarily built with Next.js. The UI Components form the foundational visual elements, assembled into Pages/Views to create user-facing screens. Client-Side Application Logic handles interactive behavior and state management within the browser, often interacting with API Routes for server-side data operations. These API Routes serve as the backend interface, orchestrating data persistence through the Data Access Layer (using Prisma) and ensuring data integrity with Schema & Validation (using Zod) across both client and server interactions.",
